Composition with A2/A3/A4 (per AC.OSS-M4.3): post-M4 the
multi-contributor PreToolUse outer list carries five inner-hook
envelopes — `objective_binding_gate.py` (A2, matcher
Edit|Write|MultiEdit), `tdd_guard.py` (A3, matcher
Edit|Write|MultiEdit), `bash_guard.py` (A4, matcher Bash),
`agent_guard.py` (A4, matcher Task), `dispatch_setup_hook.py`
(M4, matcher Task). A4 + M4 share the Task matcher and run
sequentially per Claude Code's deterministic-order semantics;
A4 runs first (refusal gate); M4 runs second (always allows).
When A4 denies (wrong-WD / method-enumerated / stale-dispatch),
Claude Code does not fire the underlying Task tool but the M4
hook still authors disk-side side-effects before the deny
short-circuits. This is acceptable per AC.DSA.4 idempotency —
a re-dispatched Task with the same AC declarations sees the
sentinel + manifest rows already in place and short-circuits
correctly. Plan §9 risk #1 documents this trade-off.

